WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.372
Seven different scans are loaded. Click a page in the list to preview it.

00:00:06.472 --> 00:00:09.373
Side by side shows the original and the result; here a double sheet becomes two pages.

00:00:09.473 --> 00:00:17.297
Original shows only the scan, Processed only the result.

00:00:17.397 --> 00:00:26.355
Slider overlays the two: drag the divider to compare before and after.

00:00:26.455 --> 00:00:35.240
Fit scales the preview to the window; switch it off to see real pixels.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:52.104
Pick other kinds of pages: a single page with punch holes, a blank page, a negative…

00:00:52.204 --> 00:00:57.566
…a sideways page (it is turned automatically, but may end upside down: the Rotate buttons fix that, see the next clip), and a phone photo.

00:00:57.666 --> 00:01:07.965
The keyboard works too: arrows and Page Up/Down move between pages, Home and End jump to the first and last.

00:01:08.065 --> 00:01:19.245
Ctrl+K opens the command palette: type a few letters and press Enter.

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:25.419
Pages that need a look are flagged: the bar shows how many, “Next” jumps to the next one (key N).

00:01:25.519 --> 00:01:37.978
The command palette can also show only the flagged pages in the list.
